## G. Mathematical conclusion

If the corrected program is run and confirms that all 2821 filtered trees have \(b(T) \le 4\), then it proves the finite claim

\[
|V(T)|=16,\quad n_2=6 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad b(T)\le 4
\]

by exhaustive computation. It does **not** prove the general implication

\[
n_2 = 2\lceil\sqrt n\rceil - 2 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad b(T)\le \lceil\sqrt n\rceil
\]

for arbitrary \(n\). It is a single verified data point for \(q=4\). No counterexample is claimed unless the program actually finds one.

